Description: avrcp: poll GetPlayStatus while a controller player is playing
 A mid-track scrub on a connected phone can never reach a D-Bus client on stock BlueZ.
 GetPlayStatus (PDU 0x30) is the only source of a REAL measured position -- MediaPlayer1.Position
 is otherwise a local wall-clock interpolation from the last notification, and unclamped, so it
 drifts past the end of the track (observed: 454520 ms on a 400346 ms track). Upstream issues
 GetPlayStatus only from the GetCapabilities response, a status change, a track change and the
 media-player-list parse, and exposes no D-Bus method that triggers one.
 .
 This adds a 2 second timer, armed when the controller player is known and dropped with the
 session, that re-reads the position while the player reports "playing". It works even against a
 target that never advertises EVENT_PLAYBACK_POS_CHANGED (0x05) -- which iOS commonly does not --
 and it also corrects the interpolation drift.
 .
 Plum-Audio relays MediaPlayer1 into Sendspin metadata roles
 (backend/scripts/sources/bluetooth_avrcp.py); a re-read that merely confirms our own anchor is
 discarded there, so the extra signals are free.
